<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CRYSTAL_INGEST_EXECUTION_1 item 4 (design/Jawa/mods/crystal_mods_inventory.md ss1/ss3/
  ss4, ratified 2026-09-10): "resolve the live Stygium-only vs repo 12-entry genstep
  discrepancy" for KOTOR_CrystalFormation, per the item's own instruction to "verify
  which genstep is actually firing before touching either."

  MEASURED, not guessed:
  1. Two copies of the KOTOR_CrystalFormation GenStepDef exist: guy762.mm.kotorcore's
     own LIVE def (1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Resources/CrystalMapGenerator.xml, still active in
     ModsConfig) and our dormant absorbed copy (Absorbed_KotorCore_CrystalMapGenerator.xml,
     NOT deployed === its own header says so, and it is confirmed absent from the deployed
     Mods/Armoury/Defs/ tree). The live def dump attributes KOTOR_CrystalFormation to
     "Star Wars KotOR Resources and Materials" (guy762.mm.kotorcore) === our copy is inert.
  2. The donor's own live groups carry `MayRequire="guy762.KotORWeapons"` on all 10
     color/medium entries (confirmed by direct read of kotorcore's shipped 1.6 XML) ===
     absent from our absorbed copy's serialization, which was captured from an EARLIER
     donor version while guy762.KotORWeapons (kotorweapons) was still active and
     un-absorbed. guy762.KotORWeapons is now RETIRED (absent from the live ModsConfig,
     confirmed) === so those 10 entries correctly evaluate to nothing today, and only
     the ungated KOTOR_StygiumCrystal entry remains. kotorcore's OWN patch file
     (1.6/Patches/Patch_SaberCrystalMapGenWhichIsStillNeededBecauseItSpawnsStygium.xml)
     confirms this is INTENTIONAL donor behavior, not drift: the genstep is kept alive
     specifically because it still spawns Stygium once the other colors' MayRequire
     goes false. Not a bug in either copy === both are internally consistent with their
     own point in time; the "12-entry vs Stygium-only" difference is exactly MayRequire
     doing its job against a mod list where kotorweapons happens to be retired.
  3. BUT: that same kotorcore patch file ALSO adds KOTOR_CrystalFormation to
     Base_Player's genSteps (plus BasePlayer_SecondArchonexusCycle and
     BasePlayer_ThirdArchonexusCycle === confirmed via the live def dump: `SELECT
     def_name FROM defs WHERE def_type='MapGeneratorDef' AND
     json_extract(json,'$.fields.genSteps') LIKE '%KOTOR_CrystalFormation%'` returns all
     three, mods=577/6fdca6f582164e2a, captured 2026-09-10T08:36:27Z). Base_Player is
     the ordinary player-colony map generator === so Stygium crystal is scattering on
     every normal Ash'karr colony map today, not gated to the Lantern Deeps at all. This
     is the item's actual live violation, independent of the MayRequire question above.

  Fix: remove KOTOR_CrystalFormation from Base_Player's genSteps. The colorful KOTOR
  family (including Stygium) remains available inside the Deeps via
  Absorbed_Kotorweapons_BiomesCaverns_Patch_KotORCrystalFormationInjector.xml's own
  addition to BMT_CrystalsGenerator, which RUT_LanternDeepGenerator.genSteps already
  includes === so this removal loses nothing, it only stops the everywhere-leak.

  DIRTY_CODE_REVIEW_STANDING_LOOP_1 fix: this originally shipped with three
  PatchOperationRemove entries, one each for Base_Player, BasePlayer_SecondArchonexusCycle
  and BasePlayer_ThirdArchonexusCycle (matching the live def dump's post-inheritance
  finding that all three carried the entry). But LoadedModManager runs ApplyPatches()
  fully BEFORE XmlInheritance.Resolve() (confirmed in source) === at patch time, Second/
  ThirdArchonexusCycle's OWN raw genSteps only ever contained their one
  ArchonexusResearchBuildings_* entry; "KOTOR_CrystalFormation" only exists in Base_Player's
  raw node, and only becomes visible on the two ArchonexusCycle children AFTER inheritance
  merges Base_Player's list into theirs (XmlInheritance.RecursiveNodeCopyOverwriteElements
  appends a List<> child's own <li>s onto the copied-down parent list, it does not
  replace it). So the Second/Third removals could never match anything and were silent,
  permanent no-ops (exactly the "patch that matches nothing logs nothing" trap) === removing
  KOTOR_CrystalFormation from Base_Player alone is both necessary and sufficient: Second/
  Third inherit Base_Player's (now-fixed) list, so the entry never reaches them either.
  Deleted the two dead operations rather than leave them implying more work was done than
  actually was.

  NOT done this pass (left for a future small follow-up, not invented here): retargeting
  BMT_CrystalsGenerator's injection off the GLOBAL GenStepDef onto a Deeps-only genstep,
  the way pyrinth/kyber were just done === per JawaWorld_BiomeMix.xml, BMT_CrystalCaverns
  is not placed on the frozen, hand-authored Ash'karr world (worldgen-gated scoring there
  only configures the disposable reference world Ash'karr is painted FROM), so this is a
  soft robustness concern (a stray quicktest/dev map), not a live leak like this one.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars KotOR Resources and Materials</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps/li[text()="KOTOR_CrystalFormation"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
